# Example Environment Variables

Copy to `.env` in root, `backend/.env`, and `frontend/.env` as needed.

## Root / General

```
# Node environment
NODE_ENV=development
```

## Backend (`backend/.env`)

```
# Database
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:password@localhost:5432/climate_db

# Server
PORT=5000
NODE_ENV=development

# Logging (false = quiet, true = verbose)
ENABLE_LOGS=false
```

## Frontend (`frontend/.env`)

```
# API Base URL (auto-detects localhost:5000 if omitted)
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5000

# Or for production:
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-backend.railway.app
```

## PostgreSQL Defaults (for reference, not an env file)

```
Host: localhost
Port: 5432
User: postgres
Password: password  (change in production!)
Database: climate_db
```

To create the database locally:
```bash
psql -U postgres -c "CREATE DATABASE climate_db;"
```
